title: 'Migrate `pallet-grandpa` from the deprecated `ValidateUnsigned` trait to `#[pallet::authorize]`'

doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `pallet-grandpa` no longer uses the deprecated `ValidateUnsigned` trait and the
    `#[pallet::validate_unsigned]` attribute. The validation of `report_equivocation_unsigned` moved
    to a `#[pallet::authorize]` callback.

    The validation semantics do not change. The callback accepts only `TransactionSource::Local` and
    `TransactionSource::InBlock`, it checks the evidence, and it builds the same transaction validity
    as before.

    Two changes affect a runtime that includes this pallet. The `EquivocationReportSystem` bound
    changed from `CreateBare<Call<T>>` to `CreateAuthorizedTransaction<Call<T>>`, and the runtime
    must put `frame_system::AuthorizeCall` in its transaction extension pipeline.
    `report_equivocation_unsigned` now needs an authorized origin, so a caller that sends it as a
    bare transaction gets `BadOrigin`.

crates:
- name: pallet-grandpa
  bump: major
- name: sp-consensus-grandpa
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-staking-async-rc-runtime
  bump: major
